    "title": "Meet the Noblesville native ship-wrecking Hulu's new reality dating show",
    "text": "March 26, 2026, 5:31 a.m. ETA Noblesville native is setting sail on the luxury love boat on Hulu's newest reality dating show.Delaney Kluger, a 2016 Noblesville High School alum who now works as a model and makeup artist in Los Angeles, will appear on the first season of \"Love Overboard,\" a reality dating competition where singles look for love on a luxury yacht sailing outside Malta. \"Call Her Daddy\" host Alex Cooper executive produced the show, and \"The Bachelor\" and \"Traitors\" alum Gabby Windey hosts.Kluger, 26, grew up in Noblesville and played on her high school volleyball team, but she always aimed to leave Indiana. At 5'-10,\" she said people always told her she should model, and after taking test shots with a local photographer, she caught the bug.Kluger set her sights on New York at 17 years old, she told IndyStar. She sold Little Caesars coupons door-to-door until she raised enough to money to stay in New York for weeks at a time, and she booked New York Fashion Week in September 2015.Kluger walked for high-profile designer Diana Putri's Diana Couture in New York, and she fell in love with the runway.\"I just felt this high,\" she said. \"I knew this was what I was meant to do.\"Kluger jetted back and forth from Indianapolis to New York until she graduated high school, then made the move to New York permanently. She lived there until late 2022, when she relocated to Los Angeles to continue modeling and build her portfolio as a makeup artist.California casting agents scouted Kluger for an upstart reality show early last year, and though she'd never considered reality TV, she figured she had nothing to lose.\"I knew almost nothing about the show going into it,\" Kluger said. \"But it was for the plot.\"\"Love Overboard\" is a \"Love Island\" meets \"Below Deck\" dating competition with a \"Wipeout\" flourish. Contestants — 16 young, sexy singles primed for Instagram glory — mingle and couple up aboard a luxury yacht sailing the Mediterranean Sea. The last couple standing wins a trip around the world worth $100,000.The added game play in \"Love Overboard,\" is a little trickier to parse out than the simple premise:The first four couples to find their spark and pair up get to enjoy the lavish boat's upper-deck amenities, while the loners roll up their sleeves and get to work as the yacht's crew. Those below deck can only earn a spot on the topside if they break up an existing couple. Contestants are eliminated when no one chooses to couple up with them during a customary re-coupling ceremony. Those who are eliminated walk the plank and plummet into the sea. Bon voyage!Kluger was cast on the show as a \"ship-wrecker\" — the \"Love Overboard\" equivalent of a hot new bombshell entering the \"Love Island\" villa to shake up the established couples. In the trailer, she suns on the deck of a dinghy speeding toward the yacht and waves to the onlooking contestants, who weren't expecting the addition.The \"bombshell\" is typically painted as a villain in shows like \"Love Overboard,\" but Kluger said that couldn't be further from who she is. Thanks to her Indiana roots, she said signature Midwest kindness has long been instilled in her.\"Love Overboard\" encourages some degree of strategy play, but Kluger said she didn't enter with any game plan or expectations. Kluger kept it real, she said, and she hopes that translates on screen.\"I stayed true to myself,\" Kluger said. \"I hope my authenticity shines through.\"All nine episodes of \"Love Overboard\" are available to stream on Hulu now.Contact IndyStar Pop Culture Reporter at hbushman@indystar.com. Follow her on X @hmb_1013.",
